{"name":"I Love to Boogie","hex":"#ffa917","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"love","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep caring for the existence of another.","Strong affection."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have a strong affection for (someone or something).","To need, thrive on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/love"},{"term":"boogie","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A piece of solid or semisolid mucus in or removed from the nostril cavity."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A style of swing dance.","Any relatively energetic dance to pop or rock music."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boogie"}],"entries":[{"title":"I Love to Boogie","blocks":[{"text":"\"I Love to Boogie\" is a song by English rock band T. Rex. It was recorded in May 1976 and released as a single in June by record label EMI. It later appeared on T. Rex's final studio album, 1977's Dandy in the Underworld. Its B-side, \"Baby Boomerang\", was taken from an earlier T. Rex album, The Slider (1972)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f0/I_Love_to_Boogie_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I_Love_to_Boogie"},{"title":"Tove Lo","blocks":[{"text":"Ebba Tove Elsa Nilsson, known professionally as Tove Lo, is a Swedish singer-songwriter. She is known for her raw, grunge-influenced take on pop music. Referring to her autobiographical lyrics, Out called Lo \"the saddest girl in Sweden\", while Rolling Stone called her \"Sweden's darkest pop export\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Tove_Lo_%282%29_By_Daniel_%C3%85hs_Karlsson.jpeg/330px-Tove_Lo_%282%29_By_Daniel_%C3%85hs_Karlsson.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tove_Lo"},{"title":"I","blocks":[{"text":"I is the ninth letter and the third vowel letter of the Latin alphabet, used in the modern English alphabet, the alphabets of other western European languages and others worldwide. Its name in English is i, plural i's or is."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Latin_letter_I.svg/330px-Latin_letter_I.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I"},{"title":"Love","blocks":[{"text":"Love encompasses a range of strong and positive emotional and mental states, from the most sublime virtue or good habit, the deepest interpersonal affection, to the simplest pleasure. An example of this range of meanings is that the love of a mother differs from the love of a spouse, which differs from the love for food. Most commonly, love refers to a feeling of strong attraction and emotional attachment."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/ToveLo.jpg/500px-ToveLo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/ToveLo.jpg/1280px-ToveLo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/ToveLo.jpg/500px-ToveLo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lo performing at the Tavastia Club in Helsinki in 2014","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AToveLo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Tove_Lo_at_Lollapalooza_Chicago_2017.jpg/500px-Tove_Lo_at_Lollapalooza_Chicago_2017.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Tove_Lo_at_Lollapalooza_Chicago_2017.jpg/1280px-Tove_Lo_at_Lollapalooza_Chicago_2017.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikime